title: 'pallet-revive: fix v4 migration double credit and partial swap'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes `pallet_revive::migrations::v4` for runtimes that switched `Config::Deposit` to
    `PGasDeposit` before scheduling v4.

    Phase 1 now clears the pallet account's `NativeDepositOf` rows and rebuilds them from
    `CodeInfoOf`. Before, it added to rows already written since the switch, crediting those code
    deposits twice. `PGasDeposit::migrate_native_to_pgas` now rolls back if minting or holding
    PGAS fails. Before, phase 2 could burn a contract's native deposit and leave nothing in its
    place, for example when the PGAS asset was not registered yet. Phase 2 now swaps only the part
    of a contract's native hold not recorded in its `NativeDepositOf` rows. Before, it swapped the
    whole hold, so payers who paid native after the switch could no longer free storage.

    `CodeInfoOf` does not record which asset paid a code deposit, so phase 1 credits every code
    deposit as native. v4 now fails at its first step, before changing any state, if the pallet
    account holds PGAS under `CodeUploadDepositReserve`. Before, it credited those deposits as
    native, so their owners were refunded from other uploaders' native deposits and the last
    owner's `remove_code` failed with `StorageRefundLocked`.

    Phase 3 now rewrites only `DeletionQueue` slots still in the legacy `TrieId` layout. Before, it
    also rewrote items queued in the new layout after the runtime upgrade, replacing their contract
    account with the zero placeholder. The deletion processor then never cleared that contract's
    `NativeDepositOf` rows, and its address could not be instantiated again
    (`PendingDepositCleanup`).

    Runtimes that already ran v4 are unaffected. Runtimes that have not:
    - Schedule v4 before the first code upload paid in PGAS. Otherwise v4 fails and the
      runtime's `FailedMigrationHandler` decides what happens next.
    - Register the PGAS asset before scheduling v4. v4 now fails at its first step if the asset
      is not registered, and fails if any contract's swap to PGAS fails; the runtime's
      `FailedMigrationHandler` decides what happens next. Before, phase 2 logged the error and v4
      completed and was recorded with nothing converted, so it never ran again.
    - If you implement `pallet_revive::WeightInfo` yourself, add `v4_clear_code_credit_step`, or
      regenerate your weights.
    - `pallet_revive::migrations::v4::Cursor` is now generic over the account id, with
      `CursorOf<T>` as the runtime's alias, and has a new `ClearCodeCredits(Option<AccountId>)`
      variant. Code that names the type should use `CursorOf<T>`; code that matches on it must
      handle the new variant.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch